324
00:18:08,440 --> 00:18:09,380
Hey, quit it!

325
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:12,670
Agumon!

326
00:18:12,753 --> 00:18:13,677
Agumon, we're out of here.

327
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:14,980
Let go!

328
00:18:16,140 --> 00:18:17,846
I'm still too scared to move.

329
00:18:17,980 --> 00:18:19,337
I've forgotten how to move.

330
00:18:19,420 --> 00:18:21,337
He's trying to break the golden noose.

331
00:18:21,420 --> 00:18:22,250
Watch it!

332
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:25,500
Let me just try to reach him.

333
00:18:27,100 --> 00:18:30,806
The only thing you'll reach is
the bottom of his footprint, Tai.

334
00:18:37,020 --> 00:18:38,420
Dig a blaster!

335
00:18:44,620 --> 00:18:48,502
With the new Dark Spirals, I will
control the whole digital world!

336
00:18:49,800 --> 00:18:51,320
Goodbye, Digi-fools!

337
00:18:51,620 --> 00:18:55,060
And say goodbye to your
pet, Agumon! Or good!

338
00:18:57,060 --> 00:18:57,897
Agumon, no!

339
00:18:57,980 --> 00:19:01,380
With the Dark Spirals in Meadow
Greymon, I am invincible!

340
00:19:03,120 --> 00:19:05,708
Meadow Greymon is the
missing link I needed!

341
00:19:05,860 --> 00:19:08,036
There's nothing that can stop me now!

342
00:19:11,460 --> 00:19:14,500
That kid is just begging
to be taking down a peg!

343
00:19:14,680 --> 00:19:16,209
But how can we defeat him?

344
00:19:16,420 --> 00:19:20,420
I let Agumon down just when he
needed me the most, and I...

345
00:19:21,180 --> 00:19:23,320
It's Yoli and Hawkmon! And Matt!

346
00:19:23,600 --> 00:19:26,820
I'm sorry about not coming
before. That's okay.

347
00:19:27,080 --> 00:19:28,962
I knew you'd show up eventually.

348
00:19:29,100 --> 00:19:32,937
Well, it's a good thing she did stay
or I never would have found you all.

349
00:19:33,020 --> 00:19:33,850
Ugh!

350
00:19:33,933 --> 00:19:37,173
Why don't you fill me in on
what's happened up until now?

351
00:19:37,840 --> 00:19:38,670
I see.

352
00:19:38,900 --> 00:19:42,135
Well, it certainly sounds
like you guys had a full day.

353
00:19:43,260 --> 00:19:44,090
That's right.

354
00:19:44,180 --> 00:19:46,160
It's all my fault. Tai?

355
00:19:46,780 --> 00:19:47,610
Huh?

356
00:19:49,340 --> 00:19:50,977
Hey, why are you hitting Tai?

357
00:19:51,060 --> 00:19:52,357
You're supposed to be friends.

358
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:55,377
And friends don't fight friends
unless they're on a boxing team,

359
00:19:55,460 --> 00:19:56,757
and that's a whole different thing.

360
00:19:56,840 --> 00:19:57,670
Hey!

361
00:19:57,753 --> 00:19:58,583
Davis, let them be!

362
00:19:59,320 --> 00:20:00,150
Tai?

363
00:20:00,980 --> 00:20:04,837
You're right. Huh? Thanks, Matt.
I needed that. Sure, any time.

364
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:05,857
I'll do it again.

365
00:20:05,940 --> 00:20:07,528
I'd really appreciate that.

366
00:20:07,860 --> 00:20:10,837
I know that I was just blaming myself for

367
00:20:10,920 --> 00:20:12,817
something that was
completely out of my control,

368
00:20:12,900 --> 00:20:17,037
and also it doesn't help if I stand
around here and feel sorry for myself.

369
00:20:17,120 --> 00:20:20,640
But now we need to focus on
how we can get Agumon back.

370
00:20:20,980 --> 00:20:23,917
Okay, we have to be willing to
fight Agumon at full strength.

371
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:27,217
I'm sure Agumon would
definitely rather be defeated

372
00:20:27,300 --> 00:20:30,157
